2026-04-06 21:01:15 - Agent_20260406205357 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 12 file construction findings in archiver/unarchiver code across 6 files. Found 1 true positive, 1 manual review, and 9 false positives.

TRUE POSITIVE: AbstractUnArchiver.java line 371 - symlink destination from archive entries (attacker-controlled) is never validated against the destination directory. The canonical path check only validates where the symlink file is placed, not where it points to. This allows path traversal via malicious symlinks in tar/zip archives pointing to arbitrary filesystem locations like /etc/passwd.

MANUAL REVIEW: DotDirectiveArchiveFinalizer.java lines 63/71 - directory paths from dot file content (s[0]) used in File construction without traversal validation. Risk depends on whether dot file content is attacker-controllable.

FALSE POSITIVES (9): All other file constructions are on the archiver (creation) side with server-controlled inputs, or are trivial File constructions (e.g., JarArchiver.findJarName just calls .getName() for basename extraction). None involve untrusted archive content being extracted to filesystem paths.
